Z||000000||Sndfr||12-16-2000||06:31 PM||||OK, stock '84 Iron Duke with no modifications... other than it has dual exhaust...<P>What are your guy's RPMs at just cruisin' steady at 75 mph on the freeway?  What are they <I>supposed</I> to be?<P>It also idles high when i start it, like around 2000.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/scorchio/sevil.gif">  <B>Matthew "Whyt Nyte" D.</B>  <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/scorchio/sgrin.gif">       <BR><B><I>84 SE</B>- automatic, rare Fender Delete option<BR>"Fender gap?  What fender gap?"</I><BR><B>(future owner of a 60's-70's Chevy muscle car)</B><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/ut2/redcap.gif">                <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/ut1/mgwhore.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cooter||12-16-2000||07:14 PM||||It depends on which transmission you have. I don't know about the automatics, but the m19 four speed at 60 MPH is right around 3,000. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||86SE||12-17-2000||01:09 AM||||The 3 speed auto turns at about 3200 at 75 MPH.<P>Final drive ratio = 3.06<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://fierodude.hypermart.net/mysig.jpg"> <BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero -- 3.4L Conversion *SUSPENDED* --<BR>Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention||||reg||1
Z||000003||bubbajoexx||12-17-2000||09:38 AM||||it should idle at 2000 at start up for about 30 seconds that is the cold start fast idle cycle.If it dose not idfle down to 600 change the temp sensor it may be defective causing the fight idle. the car if standard should rev at 3300 at 70 mph .  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/bongo.gif">  My mascot<p>[This message has been edited by bubbajoexx (edited 12-17-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Sndfr||12-17-2000||03:57 PM||||Thanks a lot guys, I was just worried cuz it seemed a little high.  Damn engines are loud as feez right behind your head!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/scorchio/sevil.gif">  <B>Matthew "Whyt Nyte" D.</B>  <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/scorchio/sgrin.gif">       <BR><B><I>84 SE</B>- automatic, rare Fender Delete option<BR>"Fender gap?  What fender gap?"</I><BR><B>(future owner of a 60's-70's Chevy muscle car)</B><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/ut2/redcap.gif">                <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/ut1/mgwhore.gif"> ||||reg||7
Z||000005||FieroJoe||12-17-2000||09:43 PM||||That's awful high for 75 I think.  My 87 2.5 coupe runs about 2700 at 75.  Last time I had it up past 3000 in 5th I was definatly going on 85-90.<P>Do I have a different final drive ratio with the 87 isuzu by any chance, thus giving this descrepancy?<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
